y custom-article mt-12"}><p className={"drop-cap"}>{"The first thing Ana Keswick did when she left her agency job in Chicago was buy a second chair for the kitchen. Not a better chair, she is quick to say, just a second one, so that whoever dropped by in the morning could stay for the length of a pot of coffee. Three years later, breakfast in her house in Hudson, New York, runs from eight until nearly eleven, and the chair is rarely empty."}</p><p>{"She is one of twelve people we followed through a year for this issue: a baker, two teachers, a retired surgeon, a couple who run a twelve-room inn, a potter, a ferry captain. None of them are rich, and none of them would call themselves minimalists. What they share is a decision, made at some point in the last decade, to stop measuring a day by how much of it was used."}</p><h2>{"The four-hour lunch"}</h2><p>{"In a valley outside Lucca, six friends have met for lunch every Saturday since 2019. The rules are short: no phones on the table, everyone brings one dish, and nobody leaves before the coffee. \"It started as a joke about how long Italians take to eat,\" says Teo Bianchi, who cooks for the group most weeks. \"Now it is the only meeting in my calendar I have never once moved.\""}</p><p>{"Long meals, it turns out, are the most common thread in the year we spent reporting this story. Ten of the twelve described one, unprompted, as the moment their week felt most like their own."}</p><blockquote>{"“We used to ask how the week went. Now we ask what the week was like. It is a different question.”"}<cite>{"Ana Keswick, Hudson, New York"}</cite></blockquote><div className={"article-wide custom-gallery"}><a href={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/1050x1400.svg"} className={"glightbox custom-post-photo"} data-gallery={"mg1-article"} data-glightbox={"description: A slow breakfast on Ana's oak table, Hudson."} aria-label={"Enlarge: breakfast on the oak table"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/1050x1400.svg"} alt={"Sourdough toast, soft-boiled eggs, figs and coffee on an oak table"} width={"1050"} height={"1400"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /></a><a href={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/1400x1050.svg"} className={"glightbox custom-post-photo"} data-gallery={"mg1-article"} data-glightbox={"description: Planting beans in the back garden in late May."} aria-label={"Enlarge: planting the back garden"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/1400x1050.svg"} alt={"A woman in a straw hat planting seedlings in a back-garden vegetable patch"} width={"1400"} height={"1050"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /></a><a href={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/1050x1400.svg"} className={"glightbox custom-post-photo"} data-gallery={"mg1-article"} data-glightbox={"description: Tea on the window seat while the rain passes."} aria-label={"Enlarge: tea on the window seat"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/1050x1400.svg"} alt={"A woman with a mug of tea on a window seat looking out at the rain"} width={"1050"} height={"1400"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /></a></div><p className={"custom-caption"}>{"Mornings in Hudson: breakfast, the bean rows, and the window seat Ana calls “the office.” Photographs by Petra Bellamy."}</p><h2>{"What a slower year costs"}</h2><p>{"Nobody we spoke to pretended the change was free. The surgeon took a 40 percent pay cut to work four days a week. The innkeepers close for all of January, which means a thin February. Ana now earns about half of what she did at the agency, and has learned to fix her own bicycle."}</p><p>{"What they bought with it is harder to put in a spreadsheet, though several of them tried. The most precise answer came from the ferry captain, who keeps a notebook of every evening he has spent on his porch since he stopped taking the late crossing: 212 last year, against 31 the year before."}</p><h3>{"Three small things they all do"}</h3><ul><li>{"Eat at least one meal a week that lasts longer than it needs to."}</li><li>{"Keep one day with nothing written in the calendar, on purpose."}</li><li>{"Walk somewhere they could have driven."}</li></ul><p>{"On our last morning in Hudson, the second chair had a visitor before eight: a neighbor returning a borrowed casserole dish, who stayed until the coffee ran out. Ana did not look at the clock once. We did, and it was ten past eleven."}</p><p className={"article-note"}><b>{"This story appears in Issue 42, The Slow Issue."}</b>{" Some names in the wider reporting have been shortened at the request of the people involved."}</p></div><div className={"mx-auto mt-14 max-w-[44rem]"}><div className={"custom-author-box"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/800x800.svg"} alt={""} width={"800"} height={"800"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><div><p className={"m-0 text-base custom-panel-soft"}>{"Written by"}</p><p className={"mt-1 mb-0 font-heading text-[2rem] leading-none"}>{"Margot Ravel"}</p><p className={"mt-3 mb-0 text-base leading-relaxed custom-panel-soft"}>{"Editor-at-Large. Margot writes about people who live a little against the clock, from Hudson, New York, where she keeps bees badly and bread well."}</p><a href={"#page=demo-magazine-1-author"} className={"btn btn-primary btn-sm mt-5"}>{"All 48 Stories "}<i className={"ph ph-arrow-right"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></div></div><ul className={"custom-topics mt-8"} role={"list"} aria-label={"Tags"}><li><a href={"#page=demo-magazine-1-category"}>{"Slow Living"}</a></li><li><a href={"#page=demo-magazine-1-category"}>{"People"}</a></li><li><a href={"#page=demo-magazine-1-category"}>{"Food"}</a></li><li><a href={"#page=demo-magazine-1-category"}>{"Issue 42"}</a></li></ul></div></div></article><section className={"pb-(--section-space)"} aria-labelledby={"mg1-related-title"}><div className={"contain